WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.733
The Google Cloud CLI is a practical
interface between Bash automation and Google

2
00:00:07.813 --> 00:00:09.302
Cloud services.

3
00:00:09.382 --> 00:00:15.976
Teams use it to list resources, publish
artifacts, deploy applications,

4
00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:23.395
update configuration, modify IAM policies,
create storage, change networking,

5
00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:30.175
start compute resources, query logs, and
support operational workflows.

6
00:00:30.255 --> 00:00:33.234
Those activities may be routine,

7
00:00:33.314 --> 00:00:37.993
but they can act directly on the cloud
control plane.

8
00:00:38.073 --> 00:00:44.668
Every CLI command runs with the account,
project, active configuration,

9
00:00:44.748 --> 00:00:51.980
region, zone, credential source, and
permissions available at execution time.

10
00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:58.548
If a script uses the wrong project, wrong
account, wrong configuration,

11
00:00:58.628 --> 00:01:03.627
wrong region, wrong zone, or unexpected
command input,

12
00:01:03.707 --> 00:01:07.323
a routine helper can affect production.

13
00:01:07.403 --> 00:01:13.998
A command that is harmless in a
development project may be high-impact in a

14
00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:15.992
production project.

15
00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:23.092
Secure Google Cloud CLI usage means
treating each script as a cloud automation

16
00:01:23.172 --> 00:01:24.236
component.

17
00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:28.676
The script should know which project it
expects,

18
00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:35.670
which account or service account it is
using, which configuration is active,

19
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:42.025
which region or zone is in scope, what
resource it is allowed to affect,

20
00:01:42.105 --> 00:01:46.147
and what output later automation will
trust.

21
00:01:46.227 --> 00:01:53.247
It should not rely on whatever local or
runner state happens to be active when it

22
00:01:53.327 --> 00:01:54.071
starts.

23
00:01:54.151 --> 00:02:02.022
The defensive goal is scoped,
least-privileged, observable Google Cloud automation.

24
00:02:02.102 --> 00:02:08.483
That means validating targets, protecting
credentials and sessions,

25
00:02:08.563 --> 00:02:13.988
invoking commands predictably, parsing
output carefully,

26
00:02:14.068 --> 00:02:20.130
guarding high-impact changes, and leaving
useful audit evidence.

27
00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:26.911
Small Bash helpers can be valuable, but if
they can change cloud resources,

28
00:02:26.991 --> 00:02:30.820
they deserve deliberate security design.
